# ArgoCD + BuildConfig: Two Independent Git Pointers

When this app is deployed from a non-`main` branch, two separate git references must be kept in sync:

| Pointer | Location | Controls |
|---------|----------|----------|
| `spec.source.targetRevision` | `gitops/signup-app.yaml` | Which branch ArgoCD reads the Helm chart from |
| `git.ref` (Helm value) | `gitops/signup-app.yaml` + `helm/values.yaml` | Which branch the **BuildConfig** clones for the Docker build |

These are independent. ArgoCD finding the Helm chart on a branch does NOT automatically tell the BuildConfig to clone from that same branch.

## Symptom

Build pod fails with:
```
error: provided context directory does not exist: signup-app
```

This means the BuildConfig cloned the wrong branch (e.g. `main`) where `signup-app/` doesn't exist yet.

## Fix

Ensure both values match the working branch in `gitops/signup-app.yaml`:

```yaml
source:
  targetRevision: signup-app   # ← ArgoCD reads Helm chart from here
  helm:
    values: |
      git:
        ref: signup-app        # ← BuildConfig clones from here — must match!
        contextDir: signup-app
```
